// Vector-quantised GeMM (FP16 -> FP32): the weights W[NxK] are stored as 16-bit codebook indices (one code per
// group of CB_D consecutive columns of a row) + NCB residual FP16 codebooks + a per-row FP16 scale:
//   W[n][g*CB_D + j] = scale[n] * sum_c codebook_c[ idx_c[n][g] ][j]      (FP16 arithmetic on Spatz)
// Spatz decodes W straight into the packed operand, O-POPE computes Z = X*W (Y = 0).  M multiple of 16.
{
    kernel: "VQGEMM"
    M: 64,
    N: 128,
    K: 128,
    CB_D: 16,
    CBN: 64,
    NCB: 2
}
